    "title": "Describe enduring possession and attachment",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk5-existence-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Describe enduring possession and attachment",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Use this relatively written-style expression to describe an enduring feature or possession. It presents the continuing quality, rather than a single event of obtaining something. A surface or object can be the initial location in a sentence with verb + 有, describing what is attached or recorded there.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "这个地方有着很长的历史。",
                "pinyin": "zhège dìfang yǒuzhe hěn cháng de lìshǐ 。",
                "meaning": "This place has a long history.",
                "audio": "2d7e4dbd67d134fe6b404b339f3388d2d40fdf3c491db0b8460524252390df79"
              },
              {
                "text": "门上写有他的名字。",
                "pinyin": "mén shàng xiě yǒu tā de míngzi 。",
                "meaning": "His name is written on the door.",
                "audio": "dfcd5f60df8639358c60f09b3f1bd3313d099905741dd43bfa5852f17ec469cb"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Words used in this pattern",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "有",
                "pinyin": "yǒu",
                "meaning": "have; there is/are",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "e05bdf8932363c5c3cef391f352fc9d20839a80952e08cb92fff972633062a8b"
              },
              {
                "text": "着",
                "pinyin": "zhe",
